        "original_id": "1eae2df2-b2f2-53a2-a813-2e741ea6f7c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Paride ed Elena, Orfeo ed Euridice, Alceste\n- People: Christoph Willibald Gluck, Ranieri de' Calzabigi, Maria Theresa\n- Places: Vienna, Burgtheater\n- Concepts: reform operas, myth of Orpheus\n\nFacts:\n- On 5 October 1762, Orfeo ed Euridice was first performed at the Burgtheater in Vienna in the presence of Empress Maria Theresa.\n- Orfeo ed Euridice is an opera by Christoph Willibald Gluck based on the myth of Orpheus with a libretto by Ranieri de' Calzabigi.\n- Paride ed Elena is the third of Gluck's so-called reform operas for Vienna, following Alceste and Orfeo ed Euridice.\n- Paride ed Elena is the least often performed of those three reform operas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
